T95-A-AV-R follow-up (card t_fcbd5cc8) — evidence, 2026-10-28

Everything below is raw output. The instrumentation (§C, §D) was a throwaway probe writing to the
app's own tmp (`NSTemporaryDirectory() + "t95gone-probe.log"`), reverted before any commit
(`git checkout -- Mattermost/`); nothing here is part of the delivered tree.

How the probe was produced (throwaway, NOT part of the deliverable) — appended to
Mattermost/UI/Native/Sidebar/ChannelSidebarCoordinator.swift:

  /// THROWAWAY: append a line to a file the host can read. The app's OWN tmp, not /tmp: an iOS
  /// simulator app cannot write /tmp (see §G).
  func t95probeFile(_ line: String) {
      let path = NSTemporaryDirectory() + "t95gone-probe.log"
      let stamped = String(format: "%.3f ", Date().timeIntervalSince1970) + line
      guard let data = (stamped + "\n").data(using: .utf8) else { return }
      if let handle = FileHandle(forWritingAtPath: path) {
          handle.seekToEndOfFile(); handle.write(data); handle.closeFile()
      } else {
          try? data.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: path))
      }
  }

  // in model(for:)'s `$groups` sink:
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE sink groups=\(groups.count) modelGroups=\(model.groups.count) saved=\(…)")
  // before each of the three decide call sites (activate, the location-change defer, the sink):
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE site=activate")   // …site=locationDefer…
  // in applyLaunchDestinationIfNeeded, at entry and at every guard/exit:
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide enter opensDest=… modelTeam=… groups=… phase=… saved=…")
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide STOP noTeam" / "STOP otherServer" / "STOP opensDest")
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide STOP noRequest entries=… saved=… decision=…")
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE decide OPEN entries=… saved=… decision=…")
  // in apply(_ location:), first statement:
  t95probeFile("T95PROBE apply loc channel=… team=… pane=… opensDest=…")

