--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§G  What is NOT evidence here, and the harness iterations that produced it
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

* `t95gone-probe-1` — setup failure, kept because it is a fact about the fixture:
  `…:116: XCTAssertTrue failed - the freshly created channel must be a row of the sidebar …`
  after 25 swipes. The sidebar renders only the rows in view on a 42-channel team; 15
  `channelSidebar.channel.*` identifiers were in the dump, the probe channel's was not. The test now
  opens through `channelSidebar.quickSwitcher` (the reader's own path to an off-screen channel).
* `t95gone-probe-5-trace` — not evidence: the first sample ran before the relaunch handshake settled
  and read the *terminating* process's last frame:
    t = 23.56s     Launch com.mattermost.ios
    1793175344.xx  MEASURE trace t=0.01 pane=true title='T95 Gone Probe' …   ← the OLD process
    error: … Failed to get matching snapshots: Application com.mattermost.ios is not running
  The test now waits for the old launch to be `.notRunning` and for the new one to be
  `.runningForeground` before its clock starts; no crash report exists for the app on this host, so
  this was a handshake, not a crash.
* `t95gone-probe-6-trace` / `t95gone-clean-2-snapshot` — not evidence: the sampling window was keyed on
  the channel directory alone, the pane covers the sidebar so no row ever appeared, the loop ran to its
  240 s ceiling and the app process vanished 131 s in (the T635 symptom on this host):
    error: … the app process died 131.3 s into the relaunch measurement (the known T635 symptom on this
    host: the process vanishes under accessibility snapshotting), so this run measured nothing.
  Trace: t=0.01 pane=true title='T95 Gone Probe' tabs=0 rows=false shell=false signIn=false |
         t=122.64 pane=false title='-' tabs=-1 rows=false shell=false signIn=false
  The window now starts at the directory *or* at the landing, whichever is first, and is bounded.
* `t95gone-clean-1` — registered only the FIRST of the three observations: a matched expected failure
  still stops a test whose `continueAfterFailure` is false. The measurement block raises it.
* `t95gone-clean-3-snapshot` — `XCTAssertNotNil(rowsAt)` refused the reproducing case (a pane covering
  the sidebar hides every row), i.e. the assertion would have made the test unable to measure the bug.
* `/tmp` is not writable from an iOS simulator app on this runtime: the parent card's
  `/tmp/t95probe-*.log` scheme leaves no file anywhere (searched the whole device dir and the app
  container). The probe here writes to `NSTemporaryDirectory()`.
* `-shellSnapshot` needs a path inside the app's own container, and the container UUID changes on every
  reinstall `xcodebuild` performs (measured: 00FF127D… → 3238125A… → C68D7419… → 5301D261… →
  C9C70DC3… → 662E185F… → E9414614… → 22CAF64F… → EC2AA1C6…). A path resolved before the run is stale
  by the time the app starts, which is why §E is a `simctl launch` rather than an XCTest relaunch.
* No APNs, no real device, no non-admin account, no iPad/regular layout: §4 of the build note lists
  what remains unvalidated.
